 "honest": [
  "one cost level by default: the sweep is about the calendar axis, and the cost signature of these cuts has been the same -8..-13bp since thirds",
  "the five days are fixed dates, not a fitted optimum: no date here is searched for and none may be read as a recommendation",
  "both calendars share one universe and one rank cache, so the only moving part is the set of decision sessions",
  "gap spread across days is a range statistic over five points, not a test",
  "descriptive census only: no gate, no verdict, no prereg, no trial count",
  "the bracket bounds are read from the E65/E66 faces (results\\e44_midmonth\\EARLYDELAY-20261020.json @20261020 / results\\e44_midmonth\\ENTRYDELAY-20261020.json @20261020), not re-burned; only the k-session arms here are new",
  "the bracket faces were burned on an older panel cutoff (20261020/20261020) than this leg (2026-10-27), so the bracket mixes one extra bar of data and is a shape reading, not a same-cutoff comparison",
  "shape labels come from a +/-2bp tolerance on three points: they describe the ladder, they are not a test and no arm here is a recommendation"
 ],
